mals, and groups according to vertex_count, face_count, and index_count.","tools/clusterfuzz.cpp exercises meshlet construction and meshopt_partitionClusters; tools/codecfuzz.cpp exercises codecs; tools/simplifyfuzz.cpp exercises simplification. None references meshopt_generateNormals."],"recommended_action":"Add a dedicated meshopt_generateNormals fuzz target or extend an appropriate geometry harness to derive bounded counts, indices, positions, output capacity, stride, and crease_angle from fuzz data. Exercise both indices == NULL and indexed modes; valid stride boundaries and varied alignment; duplicate, non-finite, collinear, and degenerate positions; repeated and adversarial valid indices; empty meshes; and multiple crease_angle values, while maintaining the documented count and buffer-size preconditions."}
